---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const updated = '21 June 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How RecConnect collects, uses, and protects your personal data."
  eventBar={false}
>
  <!-- Header -->
  <section class="relative overflow-hidden bg-brand-navy pt-36 pb-14 md:pt-44 md:pb-20 border-b border-white/10">
    <div class="absolute -top-16 -right-16 w-72 h-[26rem] bg-primary/[0.06] rotate-12 pointer-events-none" style="clip-path: polygon(20% 0, 100% 0, 80% 100%, 0 100%);"></div>
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 relative z-10">
      <p class="kicker text-primary text-[0.8rem] mb-4">Legal</p>
      <h1 class="font-display uppercase text-white text-4xl md:text-6xl leading-[0.95] mb-4">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="text-slate-400">Last updated: {updated}</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Body -->
  <section class="bg-white py-14 md:py-20">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 legal">
      <p class="lead">
        This Privacy Policy explains how RecConnect ("we", "us", "our") collects, uses, and protects
        your personal data when you visit our website or get in touch with us. We are committed to
        handling your information responsibly and in line with the UK General Data Protection
        Regulation (UK GDPR) and the Data Protection Act 2018.
      </p>

      <h2>Who we are</h2>
      <p>
        RecConnect is a professional community for the UK recruitment industry. For the purposes of
        data protection law, RecConnect is the data controller for the information described in this
        policy. You can contact us using the details in the "How to contact us" section below.
      </p>

      <h2>The information we collect</h2>
      <p>We only collect the data we need to run the website and respond to you. This falls into two categories:</p>
      <p><strong>Information you give us.</strong> If you contact us — for example by email, WhatsApp, or any
        enquiry form on this site — we receive the details you choose to share, such as your name,
        email address, phone number, company name, and the content of your message.</p>
      <p><strong>Information collected automatically.</strong> When you browse the site we use Google Analytics
        to understand how the site is used. This may include your device and browser type, the pages
        you view, how you arrived at the site, approximate location (derived from your IP address),
        and similar usage data. Google Analytics sets cookies to do this. We do not use any other
        advertising, marketing, or tracking cookies.</p>

      <h2>Cookies and analytics</h2>
      <p>
        Cookies are small text files stored on your device. The only cookies this website sets are
        those used by Google Analytics to measure and improve site performance. We do not use cookies
        for advertising or to build marketing profiles. You can block or delete cookies through your
        browser settings, and you can opt out of Google Analytics across all websites by installing
        Google's official browser add-on at
        <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>How we use your information</h2>
      <p>We use the information we collect to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>respond to your enquiries and provide the information or services you ask for;</li>
        <li>operate, maintain, and improve the website and the experience of our visitors;</li>
        <li>understand which content and pages are most useful to our community;</li>
        <li>keep the website secure and prevent misuse; and</li>
        <li>comply with our legal obligations.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Our legal basis</h2>
      <p>
        Where you contact us, we rely on our legitimate interests in responding to you and managing
        our community. Where we use analytics cookies, we rely on your consent, which you can withdraw
        at any time using the controls described above. Where we are required to keep records, we rely
        on compliance with a legal obligation.
      </p>

      <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
      <p>
        We do not sell your personal data. We share it only with service providers who help us operate
        the website, and only to the extent necessary. This currently includes Google (Google
        Analytics) for website measurement and our hosting provider for delivering the site. These
        providers process data on our behalf under appropriate safeguards. Some providers may process
        data outside the UK; where they do, we rely on the safeguards those providers put in place,
        such as the UK Addendum to the EU Standard Contractual Clauses.
      </p>

      <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
      <p>
        We keep enquiry correspondence only for as long as needed to deal with your request and for a
        reasonable period afterwards in case you contact us again. Analytics data is retained in line
        with Google Analytics' standard retention settings. We delete or anonymise data when it is no
        longer needed.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>Under UK data protection law you have the right to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>access the personal data we hold about you;</li>
        <li>ask us to correct inaccurate or incomplete data;</li>
        <li>ask us to delete your data in certain circumstances;</li>
        <li>object to or restrict how we use your data;</li>
        <li>request a copy of your data in a portable format; and</li>
        <li>withdraw consent where we rely on it.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>To exercise any of these rights, please contact us using the details below. You also have the
        right to complain to the Information Commissioner's Office (ICO) at
        <a href="https://ico.org.uk" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">ico.org.uk</a> if you are
        unhappy with how we have handled your data.</p>

      <h2>External links</h2>
      <p>
        Our website links to third-party services such as Stripe, Eventbrite, WhatsApp, LinkedIn, and
        Amazon. We are not responsible for the privacy practices of those services, and we encourage
        you to read their privacy policies before using them.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this policy from time to time. Any changes will be posted on this page with a
        revised "last updated" date.
      </p>

      <h2>How to contact us</h2>
      <p>
        If you have any questions about this policy or your personal data, please contact us:
      </p>
      <p>
        RecConnect<br />
        Briar Cottage, School Lane<br />
        Sevenoaks, Kent, TN15 0BE<br />
        Email: <a href="mailto:hello@recconnect.co">hello@recconnect.co</a>
      </p>

      <p class="disclaimer">
        This policy is provided as a general template and does not constitute legal advice. We
        recommend having it reviewed by a qualified legal professional before relying on it.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .legal { color: #334155; }
  .legal .lead { font-size: 1.15rem; line-height: 1.7; color: #1e293b; margin-bottom: 2rem; }
  .legal h2 {
    font-family: 'Anton', sans-serif !important;
    font-weight: 400 !important;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.01em;
    color: #0a0b0f;
    font-size: 1.6rem;
    margin: 2.5rem 0 0.9rem;
  }
  .legal p { line-height: 1.75; margin-bottom: 1.1rem; }
  .legal ul { list-style: disc; padding-left: 1.4rem; margin: 0 0 1.1rem; }
  .legal li { line-height: 1.7; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }
  .legal a { color: #14b8a6; text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 2px; }
  .legal a:hover { color: #0f766e; }
  .legal strong { color: #0a0b0f; font-weight: 600; }
  .legal .disclaimer {
    margin-top: 2.5rem; padding-top: 1.5rem; border-top: 1px solid #e2e8f0;
    font-size: 0.9rem; color: #64748b; font-style: italic;
  }
</style>
